  "functions": [
    "FUNC.REGEXREPLACE"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "REGEXREPLACE uses PCRE2 with numbered captures ($1, $2), rejects invalid patterns as #VALUE!, and indexes occurrences",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, REGEXREPLACE evaluates PCRE2 regular expressions, expands numbered group references ($1, $2) in replacement text, supports negative occurrence indices (e.g. -2 selects the second-from-last match), and returns #VALUE! for unclosed/invalid patterns (such as \"[\") or out-of-range occurrence indices on empty patterns. Under compatibility version 1, @REGEXREPLACE evaluates to #NAME?.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across jnt_text_formats (rows 12-15), corpus-examples regex-replace-second-from-last / regex-replace-group-order / regex-pad-components in Excel 16.0.20527.20196, and empty_regex_replace_boundaries, and matched across 4,346/4,346 full-bank REGEXREPLACE rows.",
